  "executive_briefing": "The 2026 fiscal year confirms a definitive pivot toward fiscal nationalism as jurisdictions prioritize competitive sovereignty over the waning OECD Pillar Two consensus. While the 15% global minimum tax remains a conceptual framework, the practical application is being systematically diluted by localized rate competition, cash-based rebate structures, and targeted non-taxable incentives. Trade policy volatility remains extreme, characterized by a structural conflict between executive protectionist agendas and increasingly assertive judicial oversight. Meanwhile, the digital administrative layer has hardened, with real-time transactional e-invoicing moving from innovation to a mandatory infrastructure requirement for international trade compliance.",
